<title>USA: Essex Bancorp Inc Q1 net decreases.</title>
<headline>Essex Bancorp Inc Q1 net decreases.</headline>
<dateline>NORFOLK, Va. 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997	1996</p>
<p>							     First    First</p>
<p>								 Qtr	Qtr</p>
<p>Cumulative preferred stock dividends-period end</p>
<p>							     2,210	721</p>
<p> Net income						   18	596</p>
<p> Earnings (loss) per common share		  (.36)	.04</p>
<p>		   (thousands, except per share information)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Earnings (loss) per share is computed based upon net income adjusted for cumulative but undeclared preferred stock dividends, divided by the average number of common shares outstanding.</p>
<p>Net income for the first quarter of 1996 included a $1.3 million of nonrecurring gain associated with the banks sale of its Charlotte, North Carolina, retail bank branch in March 1996.</p>
<p>The bancorp said it did not generate sufficient income to cover the $395,000 of cumulative but undeclared dividends for the first quarter of 1997 on its Series B and C preferred stock.</p>
</text>
